fl-assistant-michael-oc-rivers","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Georgia AG asks SEC to take action against LSU's 'contempt for the rules'","description":"The Georgia Attorney General blasted LSU in a letter to SEC commissioner Greg Sankey, encouraging sanctions against the Tigers, \"up to and including expulsion.\"","published":"2026-11-19T01:26:24.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/mens-college-basketball/story/_/id/50524054/georgia-ag-asks-sec-take-action-vs-lsu-expulsion","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Mark Schlabach and Pete Thamel","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Alabama running back prospect AK Dear no longer with team","description":"Alabama tailback AK Dear, a former four-star prospect who was poised to make an impact before suffering an injury in the summer, is no longer on the team.","published":"2026-11-18T19:16:16.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50523034/alabama-running-back-prospect-ak-dear-no-longer-team","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Judge questions LSU's claims the SEC 'hallucinated' citations","description":"At a hearing Wednesday in the SEC's lawsuit against LSU, a federal judge pushed back on LSU attorneys for using the word \"hallucinated\" in filing.","published":"2026-11-18T22:40:51.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50522883/judge-questions-lsu-claims-sec-hallucinated-citations","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2027 College Football Playoff National Championship odds","description":"Odds and futures to win the 2027 College Football Playoff National Championship.","published":"2026-11-18T22:17:13.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/betting/story/_/id/47664633/2027-college-football-playoff-national-championship-odds-futures","type":"Story","byline":"Doug Greenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Sources: Urban Meyer not a candidate for open Maryland job","description":"Urban Meyer has not spoken to Maryland in any formal capacity about its vacant head coaching position and is not a candidate for the job, sources told ESPN's Pete Thamel on Wednesday.","published":"2026-11-18T18:30:02.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50522632/sources-urban-meyer-not-candidate-open-maryland-job","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Davenport RB Cephus Harris III to enter transfer portal","description":"Davenport's Cephus Harris III, the leading rusher in Division II and a candidate for the Harlon Hill Trophy, plans to enter the transfer portal, he told ESPN.","published":"2026-11-18T17:52:53.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50522473/davenport-rb-cephus-harris-iii-enter-transfer-portal","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Top 25 betting lines: UGA big faves over Gamecocks, Vols slim favorites vs. LSU","description":"This week's odds and FPI predictions for South Carolina-Georgia, Tennessee-LSU and more.","published":"2026-11-18T14:36:40.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/betting/story/_/id/50498153/2026-college-football-week-12-top-25-betting-lines-odds","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Bottom 10 after Week 11: Paying tribute to our founding father","description":"The originator of celebrating football's downtrodden, former Los Angeles columnist Steve Harvey, died last week.","published":"2026-11-18T13:23:01.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50519786/bottom-10-week-11-clemson-steve-harvey","type":"Story","byline":"Ryan McGee","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4858848/anto-saka","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anto_Saka"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Anto Saka","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anto_Saka","description":"American football player (born 2004)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:37:04Z","intro":"Anto Saka (born April 12, 2004) is an American college football defensive end for the Texas A&M Aggies. He previously played for the Northwestern Wildcats.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Saka attended Loyola Blakefield in Towson, Maryland. He was rated as a four star recruit, the fourth overall player in Maryland and the 202nd overall player in the class of 2022. Saka committed to play college football for the Northwestern Wildcats over offers from other schools such as Michigan, Michigan State, Penn State, Tennessee, Toledo, USC, and Wake Forest."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"NORTHWESTERN\nAs a freshman in 2022, Saka was redshirted. In week 2 of the 2023 season, he notched his first career sack in a victory versus UTEP. In week 3 Saka tallied another sack against Duke. He finished the season with 13 tackles, five and a half sacks, and a forced fumble in 11 games played. In 2024, Saka posted 15 tackles with five being for a loss, and three and a half sacks in 11 games.\nOn January 4, 2026, Saka announced that he would enter the NCAA transfer portal.\n\nTEXAS A&M\nOn January 7, 2026, Saka announced that he would transfer to Texas A&M."}]}}